# What must never be uploaded to a Cloud Build staging bucket.
#
# `gcloud builds submit` tars this directory and uploads it. Without this file
# it falls back to .gitignore, which is close but not the same question:
# .gitignore answers "what should not be committed", and a build upload is a
# different place with different readers. Two of the entries below are the
# reason this file exists rather than being left to that fallback.

# Credentials. The updater signing key can push code to every client machine,
# and tokens.md is every client's live access token in plain text. Neither has
# any business leaving this disk.
.secrets/
.env
.env.*

# Nothing here is needed to run the tests, and together they are hundreds of
# megabytes of upload on every build.
.venv/
node_modules/
frontend/node_modules/
frontend/dist/
src-tauri/target/
builds/
tools/
demo/
.git/
.tmp/
.cache/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/

# Generated artefacts and local scratch.
docs/images/
assets/
*.mp4
*.webm
*.png
*.icns
*.ico

# Local Docker volumes. Gitignored, and large enough to dominate the upload.
docker/postgres-data/
docker/redis-data/
docker/media/
docker/backend-logs/
